From dafc4bd45c5cc45fa0a435ced1a956512fbdcafc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:51:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: let the spastic search reverse flow reach other grids

borg_flow_spastic() looks for grids next to walls where a secret door
could be found, using a reverse flow from the borg to measure how far
each grid is.  It asked for an optimized spread, but the reverse flow
starts at the borg's own grid with cost 0, and an optimized spread stops
as soon as the next cost (1) exceeds the origin's cost.  Every other
grid kept the unreachable cost and was skipped.

So the search could only ever choose the grid the borg already stood
on: from the middle of a room it found nothing and never moved, and
standing next to a wall it searched that grid and then kept choosing it
again instead of moving on.

Spread the reverse flow without optimization, as the helper's own
comment ('do NOT optimize') intends.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#146.

(cherry picked from commit f97311e5d52de4dda8d75058114c52acbdac2674)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
index 749e3858f..81c526a36 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
@@ -548,8 +548,9 @@ bool borg_flow_spastic(bool bored)
         return false;
     }
 
-    /* Reverse flow */
-    borg_flow_reverse(250, true, false, false, -1, false);
+    /* Reverse flow, not optimized: it starts at the borg's own grid (cost 0)
+     * and an optimized spread stops before reaching any other grid. */
+    borg_flow_reverse(250, false, false, false, -1, false);
 
     /* Scan the entire map */
     for (y = 1; y < AUTO_MAX_Y - 1; y++) {
